    "text": "A simple harmonic oscillator of angular frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is acted upon by an external force <math><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>.&#160;</mo></mrow></mrow></math>If the oscillator is at rest in its equilibrium position at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> its position at later times is proportional to:",
